Z||000003||theogre||06-01-99||07:37 AM||||you might also want to look at Centerforce.  <A HREF="http://www.centerforce.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centerforce.com</A>  they have a nice package. I've not used one in Fiero yet, but have put them in a number of other cars/trucks that take far more abuse than most people would ever give a vehicle short of wrecking it. I've never seen one fail unless it was installed wrong, or just plain worn out.<p>No mater what set you use, get the fly wheel turned. if it's showing any damage at all replace it. I know that seem obvious, but a huge number of people skip it.
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||06-01-99||08:31 AM||||Well, LUK is very hard to get hold of.  If anybody needs to know the distributer in Indianapolis, let me know.  This information wouldn't be any good for other towns.  <p>Although, I have a contact with LUK now if anybody wants to know.
